# ═══ META-LESSONS ═══
L1: The "substrate present, criterion non-substrate" pattern is the most common cause of stuck PARCIAL rows. Almost every 0.80 row is PROSE-PARTIAL — the gap is the held-below criterion, not the implementation.

L2: 0.5ed closed 4 rows because all 4 were spec_kb.yaml text edits. The work was TEXT (spec correction with evidence), not CODE (substrate). This is the cheapest possible L3 wave.

L3: The P3-NO-OP audit pattern is now fully instrumented: 5 orphan counters found across 3 audit waves. The pattern is consistent: counter DEFINED, never CALLED. Future audits should treat orphan counters as a standard finding class.

L4: 85.3% with 34/37 CONFORME is a strategic milestone. The remaining 1 PARCIAL (formal-verify 0.65) is the ONLY strategic gap left in the CAH roadmap; closing it requires the SMT proof-assistant epic (~10ed, ES1 P1+P4). The remaining 2 AUSENTE are non-goals (multimodal) or A-prefix (negligible).
